---
import Base from '~/layouts/Base.astro';
import Card from '~/components/Card.astro';
import BulkReview from '~/components/islands/BulkReview.tsx';
---

<Base title="review everything · console" breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'console', href: '/console/' }, { label: 'review' }]}>
  <section class="mb-6">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Review everything</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-muted text-base max-w-3xl">
      Visibility and veto in one place: episodes and topics one at a time,
      bless as a quality signal or reject to stop a note flowing (nothing
      in the pipeline waits on a verdict). Anchor-coverage gaps
      and open ingestion reports are read-only elsewhere
      (<a href="/console/" class="text-accent hover:underline">/console/</a>
      and <code>/drift/&lt;repo&gt;/</code>); closing them is in-session work.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Card eyebrow="01 / manual" title="Walk one at a time" right="you read · you decide" padded={false}>
    <BulkReview client:load />
  </Card>

  <Card eyebrow="02 / how this works" title="What each verdict does">
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-sm text-muted space-y-1 max-w-3xl">
      <li><strong>approve</strong> &rarr; POSTs to <code>/api/episode/&lt;slug&gt;/review</code> or <code>/api/topic/&lt;r&gt;/&lt;s&gt;/review</code>, which stamps <code>reviewed_by_human:</code> on the file and drops it from the queue.</li>
      <li><strong>reject</strong> &rarr; same endpoint with <code>verdict=reject</code> plus your note. The note is stamped on the file; rewriting it is a session's job (<code>/revise &lt;topic&gt;</code>).</li>
      <li><strong>anchor gaps</strong> &rarr; surfaced by <code>/api/anchor-coverage</code>, fixed by adding <code>path:NNN</code> citations in-session.</li>
      <li><strong>drift</strong> &rarr; the deterministic drain re-anchors line shifts on its own; a report you still see needs judgment, so resolve it in-session per CLAUDE.md §4.</li>
    </ul>
  </Card>
</Base>
